Yes, Slash'em is both harder and easier. Doppelgagner monks are probably  
one of the easiest combinaison in Slash'em. As a matter of fact, I've stop  
playing Doppelgangers when randomly rolling a character.
There are tremendous amount of loot, including the black-market, and the  
Mall is often a big help in the early game (I almost never do the mines  
first in Slash'em).

On the other hand, I do find the early and mid-game harder than in  
Nethack. Monsters are a bit tougher (I find) and there are a lot of  
special level that trick me into believing I can do it before being caught  
deep surrounded by monsters. Vecna is usually a real pain better left for  
later even if the hand is of great help.

You can try Vampires. Their constant thirst make them hard to play in the  
early game, especially if you're more a wizard than a fighter.
The two specialized wizards (mages) are also interesting. Since they don't  
have the hungerless casting of true wizards, they are really hard to play  
in the early game (basically, they're wizard but can't cast spells...) and  
even if you cast, summoning spheres is not as good as force bolt.  
[actually, I considered the no hungerless casting to be a problem rather  
than a feature and wrote a patch to solve this, see  
http://bamgames.free.fr/ but I'm not satisfied with the patch, it's too  
powerfull currently, and have ideas to improve it (and use it to  
differentiate roles a bit more). Ideas, I'll prçobably never implement as  
